## 13. Data-model acceptance criteria

The data model is ready for initial implementation when it can demonstrate that:

1. A profile can own a study session.
2. A session can contain multiple rounds.
3. A round can contain multiple ordered sources.
4. A source can become unavailable without deleting derived history.
5. Multiple analysis attempts can exist for one round.
6. Failed, timed-out, insufficient-evidence, and completed analyses remain
   distinguishable.
7. An analysis preserves its exact source hashes and rule versions.
8. Measurements, observations, evidence, and score contributions remain
   distinguishable.
9. Country and regional candidate totals use the same contribution structure and
   can be explained independently.
10. A checkpoint references one immutable analysis.
11. Player guesses and actual locations remain separate.
12. Current guess, verified actual location, and evaluation are selected through
    authoritative same-round pointers.
13. Ground-truth corrections create new evaluations rather than rewriting old
    evaluations.
14. Country and regional evaluation can be unevaluated independently.
15. Current summaries exclude superseded evaluations by default.
16. Learning insight snapshots identify their source scope and rule version.
17. Historical analyses remain interpretable after newer scoring or knowledge
    versions are added.

---

## 14. Summary

GeoMeta's data model is centered on traceability and historical integrity.

The core chain is:

```text
Profile
  -> StudySession
    -> Round
      -> Source
        -> Analysis
          -> Measurement
            -> Observation
              -> Evidence
                -> CandidateScore
                  -> ScoreContribution
      -> Checkpoint
      -> PlayerGuessRevision
      -> ActualLocationRevision
      -> Evaluation
  -> LearningInsightSnapshot
```

This structure supports the product's central promise: GeoMeta should not only
produce a location ranking, but preserve how that ranking was produced, what the
player guessed, what the actual location was, and what can responsibly be learned
from the result.